mm38 boundary parks survive the idle heal, on top of mm37 (wasmtime-nn-ggml-mm37-end-parks.patch: wasmtime 2936ad79).
Same tree, cargo cache and command (~/Projects/enclave-runtime-park/build-in-ns.sh; a no-change build reproduced
2936ad79 again on 2026-10-19) -> wasmtime 2efa336b, Shield release 58a0e7bd (= d7cf9d7a + rt/wasmtime).

The idle heal (the last session ends and every park has aged past its TTL) used to drop every park and clear the
pool. Boundary parks are the deployment's standing prompt prefix, parked once by its boot warm-up; after a quiet night
(PREFIX_TTL_S, 6 h) the first request to end - eyesoff's /warmup model probe on a page load - wiped them, and the
sign-in re-read the whole ~6.5K-token prefix. KV runs (llamacpp-kv-runs.patch) already stop high-standing cells from
taxing every decode step, so the heal now drops only the stale turn parks and leaves boundary parks in place; the pool
clears outright only when no boundary park stands. Rig (Qwen3.5-0.8B MTP, PREFIX_TTL_S=30): /warmup after the idle
wait found every variant covered (1.66 s) where 2936ad79 re-prefilled (6.3 s, "covered 0 (parks [])").

